        "id": 1042828
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T01:22:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this works, and it\u0027s probably the fastest alternative. https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/cacheflush.2.html may also work. I would at least try to use that as fallback below.\n\nThe current approach has the disadvantage that it doesn\u0027t really cover RISC-V.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "47fc4c7603ccb8cae401c6bb4fec1044365b8a8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f42c2bf7_52ee5f19",
        "filename": "core/jni/com_android_internal_util_ArrayUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T02:01:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no cacheflush system call on AArch64, x86_64, i386, or RISC-V.  It does exist on 32-bit ARM, so it could be used there.\n\nI couldn\u0027t find any solution for RISC-V.  Let me know if you are aware of any.  It may need a new RISC-V extension to be developed.",
      "parentUuid": "6b0bc281_67e53eaa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "47fc4c7603ccb8cae401c6bb4fec1044365b8a8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba4a7936_7bdf124c",
        "filename": "core/jni/com_android_internal_util_ArrayUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-08T22:52:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yeah, there\u0027s a __riscv_flush_icache(), but nothing for the data cache.",
      "parentUuid": "f42c2bf7_52ee5f19",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "47fc4c7603ccb8cae401c6bb4fec1044365b8a8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "00e39406_92a48302",
        "filename": "core/jni/com_android_internal_util_ArrayUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T21:17:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The cacheflush system call on arm32 actually differs from the cacheflush(2) system call that is documented in the linux man-pages project.  Based on the code, it actually has the prototype `int cacheflush(unsigned long start, unsigned long end, int flags)`, where `flags` must be 0 and it always flushes the icache (not dcache).  So it does not appear to be useful here.  I have documented this in the code.\n\nFor RISC-V, the cbo.clean instruction from the Zicbom extension should eventually work, but it is not ready to be used yet.  I have added the code that uses it, but left it commented out for now.",
      "parentUuid": "ba4a7936_7bdf124c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "47fc4c7603ccb8cae401c6bb4fec1044365b8a8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4203b40_0a24f542",
        "filename": "core/jni/com_android_internal_util_ArrayUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 76,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042828
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T01:22:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is OK, though it reads a little strange. This is a C23 (C24?) function. memset should be fine if CleanDataCache is not known to the compiler to be a no-op.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "47fc4c7603ccb8cae401c6bb4fec1044365b8a8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bafd4b70_081ef9ad",
        "filename": "core/jni/com_android_internal_util_ArrayUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 76,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T21:17:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CleanDataCache will be a no-op on architectures that do not implement it.",
      "parentUuid": "c4203b40_0a24f542",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "47fc4c7603ccb8cae401c6bb4fec1044365b8a8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66dbdca8_df688fa8",
        "filename": "core/jni/com_android_internal_util_ArrayUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 93,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042828
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T01:22:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Again, I\u0027d be more paranoid and add some sort of check, ideally only for eng builds (?), that this is not a copy. Another option is to use GetPrimitiveArrayCritical(), which would exclude the GC if the object were movable, but is similar for nonmovable objects (Android only).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 93,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 93,
        "endChar": 73
      },
